{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>El</b>, ki — two joined forms. [The vav and zayin refer to the two letters that form the prefix כִּי (kaf-yod), though the comment is terse and the reference may be to a different pairing.]" "<b>Titnadar</b> — be adorned in garment and chariot like him." "<b>And in the place of great ones</b> — where they stand, do not stand there."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:36.622775203Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}